From: Jerrod <jerrod.uno@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: clamp scaled texture mip copies to the host mip size

With draw resolution scaling, a scaled-resolve texture is created at guest
size * scale, so D3D12 sizes its mips as max((size * scale) >> level, 1).
The load path lays out the copy buffer as max(size >> level, 1) * scale.
Once a dimension reaches 1 these differ (Crackdown 2 resolves a mipmapped
256x1 RGBA8 texture: at 2x mip 1 is 256x1 on the host, 256x2 in the
footprint), and levels below the packed tail were copied with no source
box, so CopyTextureRegion ran past the destination
(COPYTEXTUREREGION_DSTREGIONOUTOFBOUNDS), the command list failed to
close and ExecuteCommandLists removed the device (DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL)
right after the boot logo. Copy only the host mip's extent, like the packed
tail branch and the Vulkan backend (imageExtent) already do, clamped to
the footprint, which is the smaller one for some non-power-of-two sizes.
---
diff --git a/src/graphics/d3d12/texture_cache.cpp b/src/graphics/d3d12/texture_cache.cpp
index 2be0e8e..ffe3cec 100644
--- a/src/graphics/d3d12/texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/d3d12/texture_cache.cpp
@@ -1920,6 +1920,28 @@ bool D3D12TextureCache::LoadTextureDataFromResidentMemoryImpl(Texture& texture,
                      host_block_height);
       source_box.back = source_box.front + std::max(depth >> level, uint32_t(1));
       source_box_ptr = &source_box;
+    } else if (texture_resolution_scaled) {
+      // The footprint is max(guest size >> level, 1) * scale, but the host
+      // texture was created at guest size * scale, so its mips are
+      // max((size * scale) >> level, 1), smaller once a dimension reaches 1
+      // (a 256x1 resolve at 2x: mip 1 is 256x1 on the host, 256x2 in the
+      // footprint). For non-power-of-two sizes the footprint can instead be
+      // the smaller one (65 at 2x: mip 1 is 65 on the host, 64 in the
+      // footprint), so copy the overlap of the two.
+      const D3D12_SUBRESOURCE_FOOTPRINT& footprint = location_source.PlacedFootprint.Footprint;
+      source_box.left = 0;
+      source_box.top = 0;
+      source_box.front = 0;
+      source_box.right = std::min(
+          footprint.Width,
+          rex::align(std::max((width * texture_resolution_scale_x) >> level, uint32_t(1)),
+                     host_block_width));
+      source_box.bottom = std::min(
+          footprint.Height,
+          rex::align(std::max((height * texture_resolution_scale_y) >> level, uint32_t(1)),
+                     host_block_height));
+      source_box.back = std::min(footprint.Depth, std::max(depth >> level, uint32_t(1)));
+      source_box_ptr = &source_box;
     } else {
       source_box_ptr = nullptr;
     }
